  "description": "The account break and the WS-FIRST-TIME guard that suppresses it. :181 compares WS-CURR-CARD-NUM with TRAN-CARD-NUM - both PIC X(16) - and :182 writes account totals only when WS-FIRST-TIME is 'N', so the very first record breaks no account even though the card number certainly changed from the initial spaces. Four records over three cards produce exactly two account-total pairs, each an REPORT-ACCOUNT-TOTALS line followed by a TRANSACTION-HEADER-2 rule, and the third account's total is discarded unwritten when the run ends.",
